index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..2fe7c715c8752f5dab284f3e08bf248443148c55
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,207 @@
+# arXiv:1710.05491 — Balanced Judicious Bipartition generator
+
+> **Build status:** the generator and local gates G1–G8 pass. It is not yet
+> shippable: all bare, structural-hint, and placebo oracle calls received
+> OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” G9(b) therefore has no scored
+> attempts and fails closed. No API error is counted as a model failure.
+
+| Profile field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Track | **B** — no-tool compression; an efficient algorithm is disclosed |
+| Native domain | combinatorics |
+| Object regime | finite discrete |
+| Computational core | linear algebra over GF(2) |
+| Certificate | exact symbolic affine-parity rule |
+| Intuition | change of variables: reverse concealed basis changes |
+| Domain essentiality | native |
+| Reduction | none |
+
+## What the family is
+
+The source is Lokshtanov, Saurabh, Sharma, and Zehavi,
+[*Balanced Judicious Partition is Fixed-Parameter Tractable*](https://arxiv.org/abs/1710.05491).
+Section 1 defines BJB: given a multigraph and `mu,k1,k2`, partition the vertices
+into an ordered pair `(V1,V2)` with `|V1|=mu` and at most `k_i` edges induced by
+side `i`.
+
+An instance here is an exact, succinct Cayley multigraph on `GF(2)^n`. Generator
+mask `g` joins every `x` to `x XOR g`, with a stated parallel-edge
+multiplicity. The solver returns a nonzero hexadecimal mask `w` and a phase
+bit; these denote `V1={x: parity(w AND x)=phase}`. Verification checks every
+binary inner product `w.g`. If all are one, every edge crosses the partition;
+every nonconstant parity rule also selects exactly half of the vector space.
+
+Generation starts from a known covector, carries it through three invertible
+column-update tours, and adds odd sums of the resulting basis generators. It
+never solves the graph it emits. The basis spans the group, so the graph is
+connected. Proposition 1 then guarantees that the two phase choices are its
+only bipartitions.
+
+## Why Track B is honest
+
+This is not a Track-A distributional-hardness claim. Theorem 1 proves general
+BJB FPT in `k=k1+k2`, with running time `2^{k^{O(1)}} |V|^{O(1)}`. Section 3
+builds that algorithm from Odd Cycle Transversal, annotated bipartite BJB,
+connected components, a highly connected tree decomposition, and dynamic
+programming. On this more special succinct `k=0` family, ordinary GF(2)
+Gauss–Jordan elimination is enough: it succeeds 8/8 in `O(n^3)` and at shipping
+`n=96` averages **408,840 scalar-bit operations and 0.001 s**. Explicit BFS
+would instead touch `2^96` vertices.
+
+The compact construction-specific route reverses the three displayed
+coordinate tours on an all-one right-hand side. It costs exactly **285 XORs**.
+That is below the 300-operation cap but is not a reliable unaided mental
+calculation. The gap between dense elimination (or exponential explicit
+coloring) and this reversible change of variables is the Track-B claim.
+
+## Worked demo
+
+This is the complete rendering of `make_instance(n=6, extras=2, layers=3,
+seed=0)`:
+
+```text
+BALANCED JUDICIOUS BIPARTITION ON A SUCCINCT MULTIGRAPH
+
+All arithmetic in the graph definition is exact. A vertex is an n-bit
+vector, identified with its integer x in 0..2^n-1 (bit 0 is least
+significant). For integers a,b, XOR is bitwise exclusive-or, AND is
+bitwise conjunction, and parity(a) is the number of 1-bits modulo 2.
+
+Here n=6; the graph has every vertex x in 0..63.
+For each line MASK MULTIPLICITY below and every vertex x, the graph has
+MULTIPLICITY parallel undirected edges between x and x XOR MASK. Each
+unordered pair is included once. MASK is hexadecimal. There are no
+other edges. The masks on the listed lines are distinct and nonzero.
+
+GENERATOR MASKS AND PARALLEL-EDGE MULTIPLICITIES:
+2c 1001
+26 1006
+1f 1005
+13 1008
+31 1007
+2b 1004
+1e 1003
+0f 1002
+
+The following coordinate tours are part of the exact instance metadata.
+Every tour is a permutation of bit positions 0..n-1, written left to
+right; their order and direction matter.
+COORDINATE TOURS:
+4 2 1 0 5 3
+4 0 1 5 2 3
+5 3 0 2 1 4
+
+A submitted pair MASK_HEX, PHASE denotes the ordered partition
+V1={x : parity(MASK_HEX AND x)=PHASE}, V2=all other vertices.
+MASK_HEX must have exactly ceil(n/4) lowercase hexadecimal digits and
+represent a nonzero n-bit integer. PHASE must be 0 or 1.
+
+Find such a partition with |V1| exactly mu=32, with at most
+k1=0 edges wholly inside V1 and at most k2=0 edges
+wholly inside V2. Parallel edges count separately. Order matters because
+the requested size and the two edge bounds belong to V1 and V2 as written.
+
+Give your final answer inside <answer></answer> tags, as
+MASK_HEX, PHASE.
+Example shape: <answer>01, 0</answer>
+Output nothing else inside the tags.
+```
+
+The answer is `<answer>2e, 0</answer>` and `verify` returns `(True, "ok")`.
+Changing the mask to `2f` returns `(False, "a Cayley generator creates
+forbidden internal edges")`. A person can solve the demo on paper by reversing
+15 bit updates; that is why `demo` is genuinely hand-scale.
+
+## Presets
+
+| Preset | Dimension | Extra generators | Tour XORs | Vertices | Status |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| demo | 6 | 2 | 15 | 64 | hand example |
+| easy | 64 | 8 | 189 | 2^64 | bare oracle run blocked before scoring |
+| medium | 80 | 12 | 237 | 2^80 | untested by oracle |
+| hard | 96 | 16 | 285 | 2^96 | provisional shipping preset |
+
+No preset was rejected by a solver or an attack. `hard` is named by
+`SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY`, but it must not enter a release until the oracle runs
+finish and G9 passes.
+
+## Gate measurements
+
+| Gate | Result | Measurement |
+|---|---|---|
+| G1 | pass | 12/12 planted certificates verify; JSON round-trip included |
+| G2 | pass | 5/5 corruptions rejected with 5 distinct reasons |
+| G3 | pass | tagged answer recovered through prose and a Markdown fence |
+| G4 | pass | 0/200,000 structure-aware guesses; space = 158,456,325,028,528,675,187,087,900,670 |
+| G5 | pass | shipping density 0/200,000; exactly 2 valid affine rules; demo brute force counts 2 |
+| G6 | pass | four attacks all 0/8; reference elimination 8/8 at 408,840 mean operations |
+| G7 | pass | dimension doubles 96→192 while the answer remains 2 atoms and verifies |
+| G8 | pass | 80/80 invariance checks, 60/60 carried witnesses, 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
+| G9 | **fail closed** | 30 chars, 8 estimated tokens, 2 atoms, 285 operations fit; hinted oracle gate has 0 scored attempts |
+
+The four failing attacks are coordinate-frequency outlier, greedy column
+majority, 256 random affine restarts, and the in-context forward-tour ansatz.
+All graph vertices have the same degree, so there is no planted vertex
+population for an outlier test to distinguish.
+
+## Oracle loop
+
+The harness wrote every transcript. The bare run stopped after four redraws;
+all were infrastructure errors, not attempts.
+
+| Arm/preset | Models drawn | Seeds | Scored solved/attempts | Outcome |
+|---|---|---|---:|---|
+| bare/easy | Claude Sonnet 5 ×3; Grok 4.6 ×1 | 1370186612, 1064368870, 1252471701, 1477188379 | 0/0 | HTTP 403 key limit; no verdict |
+| hinted/hard | Gemini 3.1 Pro ×3; GPT-5.6 Terra ×1 | 2043928336, 62329565, 503505585, 58303656 | 0/0 | HTTP 403 key limit; no verdict |
+| placebo/hard | Claude Sonnet 5 ×2; Grok 4.6 ×2 | 2037915462, 2052941973, 812740053, 154316565 | 0/0 | HTTP 403 key limit; no verdict |
+
+## G9 arms
+
+| Arm | Solved / scored attempts | Transcript |
+|---|---:|---|
+| bare | 0/0 | `llm_loop_transcript.jsonl` (four 403 errors) |
+| structural hint | 0/0 | `g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl` (four 403 errors) |
+| placebo hint | 0/0 | `g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl` (four 403 errors) |
+
+Hinted minus placebo is **undefined**, because neither arm has a scored
+attempt; the module records `0.0` only as a neutral machine-readable
+placeholder. Nothing can yet be concluded about whether the hint carries useful
+structural information. The answer-size and route caps do pass: **30
+characters, 8 estimated tokens, 2 atoms, 285 exact operations**.
+
+## Use
+
+```python
+from gen_1710_05491 import DIFFICULTY, make_instance, parse_answer, verify
+
+inst = make_instance(seed=7, **DIFFICULTY["hard"])
+assert verify(inst, inst["answer"]) == (True, "ok")
+raw = f"reasoning... <answer>{inst['answer'][0]}, {inst['answer'][1]}</answer>"
+assert verify(inst, parse_answer(raw))[0]
+```
+
+After OpenRouter quota is restored, rerun the bare harness from this directory,
+then rerun structural and placebo copies separately. Only after all evidence
+passes should the repository-root emission command be used:
+
+```bash
+python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_1710_05491.py
+bash scripts/emit.sh 1710.05491 20 hard
+```
+
+## Caveats
+
+The family is easy with software by design: GF(2) elimination is the disclosed
+reference algorithm, and recognizing the reversible tours exposes an even
+shorter route. The paper assumes an explicitly represented multigraph, whereas
+this module gives the exact graph succinctly by Cayley generators; therefore
+the `2^n` BFS comparison is a statement about decompression, not a new
+complexity consequence of Theorem 1. The 0/200,000 guess rate samples only the
+declared affine-rule language; it does not measure informed algebraic attacks.
+
+The canonical key is complete for the module's multiplicity-distinguished
+linear presentation, but it is not a general multigraph isomorphism canonizer.
+The panel does not test SAT/ILP encodings, code-equivalence attacks, or an LLM
+with arithmetic tools. Most importantly, no cross-vendor hardness claim can be
+made until the current external 403 block is removed and all three oracle arms
+produce scored attempts.
