+All graph vertices have the same degree, so there is no planted vertex
+population for an outlier test to distinguish.
+
+## Oracle loop
+
+The harness wrote every transcript. The bare run stopped after four redraws;
+all were infrastructure errors, not attempts.
+
+| Arm/preset | Models drawn | Seeds | Scored solved/attempts | Outcome |
+|---|---|---|---:|---|
+| bare/easy | Claude Sonnet 5 ×3; Grok 4.6 ×1 | 1370186612, 1064368870, 1252471701, 1477188379 | 0/0 | HTTP 403 key limit; no verdict |
+| hinted/hard | Gemini 3.1 Pro ×3; GPT-5.6 Terra ×1 | 2043928336, 62329565, 503505585, 58303656 | 0/0 | HTTP 403 key limit; no verdict |
+| placebo/hard | Claude Sonnet 5 ×2; Grok 4.6 ×2 | 2037915462, 2052941973, 812740053, 154316565 | 0/0 | HTTP 403 key limit; no verdict |
+
+## G9 arms
+
+| Arm | Solved / scored attempts | Transcript |
+|---|---:|---|
+| bare | 0/0 | `llm_loop_transcript.jsonl` (four 403 errors) |
+| structural hint | 0/0 | `g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl` (four 403 errors) |
+| placebo hint | 0/0 | `g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl` (four 403 errors) |
+
+Hinted minus placebo is **undefined**, because neither arm has a scored
+attempt; the module records `0.0` only as a neutral machine-readable
+placeholder. Nothing can yet be concluded about whether the hint carries useful
+structural information. The answer-size and route caps do pass: **30
+characters, 8 estimated tokens, 2 atoms, 285 exact operations**.
+
+## Use
+
+```python
+from gen_1710_05491 import DIFFICULTY, make_instance, parse_answer, verify
+
+inst = make_instance(seed=7, **DIFFICULTY["hard"])
+assert verify(inst, inst["answer"]) == (True, "ok")
+raw = f"reasoning... <answer>{inst['answer'][0]}, {inst['answer'][1]}</answer>"
+assert verify(inst, parse_answer(raw))[0]
+```
+
+After OpenRouter quota is restored, rerun the bare harness from this directory,
+then rerun structural and placebo copies separately. Only after all evidence
+passes should the repository-root emission command be used:
+
+```bash
+python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_1710_05491.py
+bash scripts/emit.sh 1710.05491 20 hard
+```
+
+## Caveats
+
+The family is easy with software by design: GF(2) elimination is the disclosed
+reference algorithm, and recognizing the reversible tours exposes an even
+shorter route. The paper assumes an explicitly represented multigraph, whereas
+this module gives the exact graph succinctly by Cayley generators; therefore
+the `2^n` BFS comparison is a statement about decompression, not a new
+complexity consequence of Theorem 1. The 0/200,000 guess rate samples only the
+declared affine-rule language; it does not measure informed algebraic attacks.
+
+The canonical key is complete for the module's multiplicity-distinguished
+linear presentation, but it is not a general multigraph isomorphism canonizer.
+The panel does not test SAT/ILP encodings, code-equivalence attacks, or an LLM
+with arithmetic tools. Most importantly, no cross-vendor hardness claim can be
+made until the current external 403 block is removed and all three oracle arms
+produce scored attempts.
